tmp/
node_modules

# A skill belonging to this project lives here as a real folder, committed. A
# source's skill or a private one is a symlink holding this machine's path, which
# would load nothing on the next machine, so these two lines ignore links and
# track folders. Which skills are on lives in "skills" in .flow/settings.json.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/*/

# .flow/ is Flow's working store: tickets, groundwork, the inbox, the handoff.
# It is committed. A hidden folder invites a blanket ignore, and one stray line
# here loses every ticket the project has.
#
# One file inside it belongs to the machine rather than the project.
# flow git allow --project writes an unlock with a clock on it, and the guard
# deletes that entry once the clock runs out. Committed, it would be one commit
# saying git writes are on and another an hour later saying they are off.
.flow/settings.local.json
